  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">The 28 bifolia are bound in a three-hole pamphlet binding featuring a brown paper accordion binding, sewn with orange linen thread.  According to Aly, "the binding plays a powerful role in producing my artist's books, the look and presence of these bindings is an integral part of my work and they are linked to the content and aesthetics. The final pieces encourage the viewer to interact with the work."</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Bound in beige handmade flax paper over boards; rectangular white paper title label, with title printed in English and Arabic, mounted in a rectangular niche stamped in upper board; front and rear pastedowns are brown paper.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">An edition of 40.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">LC has copy number 27.</subfield>
    <subfield code="5">DLC</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">The twenty-eight letters of the Arabic alphabet, each laser-cut on the two leaves of a bifolium.  The movable accordion binding allows the reader to explore and interact with the letters.</subfield>
  </datafield>
